{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Moses was a shepherd.</b> Everyone about whom it says <b>was</b>, saw a new world. <b>And Moses was a shepherd</b> — yesterday he fled from his master, now he is drowning his master in water.]" "<b>Priest of Midian.</b> Prince of Midian.]" "<b>Behind the wilderness.</b> There grass is found, pasture for livestock." "<b>Chorevah.</b> It is near Egypt, a three-day journey, as it says, 'Let us go, please, a three-day journey into the wilderness.' And Mount Sinai is called so on account of the event of the bush (sneh)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The bracketed text and closing bracket appear in the source; preserved as found.", 1 "Closing bracket preserved from source; no opening bracket in this comment.", 3 "The wordplay Sinai/sneh is implicit in the Hebrew; the parenthetical is added to make the etymology visible."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:55.703877528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}